layout: base.njk
title: Bin Collections
description: Bin collection days for Church, Rous, Ab, Atch and Sheriffs Lench and Harvington, what goes in which bin, and where the nearest tip and recycling banks are.
---
<main class="container">

  <section>
    <h1>Bin Collections</h1>
    <p class="lead">Collection days across the six villages, and what goes in which bin.</p>
    <p><span class="datestamp">Page updated {{ updated | longDate }}</span></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Next collections</h2>
    <div class="grid" id="bin-grid">
      <p class="mut">Collection days are shown here automatically — if nothing appears, <a href="https://www.wychavon.gov.uk/waste-and-recycling/bins-and-collections" target="_blank" rel="noopener">check your bin day at Wychavon</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <p class="small mut">Bins out by {{ bins.putOutBy }} on the day, at the boundary of your property nearest the road, with the lid closed — crews may leave a bin whose lid won't shut. Five villages are collected on a Monday; Rous Lench is collected on the Friday of the same week.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What goes where</h2>

    <h3>Green bin — recycling</h3>
    <p>Everything must be <strong>clean, dry and loose</strong>. A bin with black sacks inside won't be collected, even if the sacks are full of recycling.</p>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Cans, tins and foil</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Food and pet food tins, drinks cans, aerosols, sweet and biscuit tins, metal jar lids. Clean aluminium foil and foil trays — scrunch foil into a ball, or small pieces get lost in sorting. Aluminium tubes such as tomato purée.</p>
        <p class="small mut mt0">No saucepans, cutlery or tools; no foil pouches or coffee pods; don't flatten cans.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Glass bottles and jars</h3>
        <p class="mt0">All colours. Lids can stay on, labels can stay on. Also fragrance bottles and make-up or moisturiser jars.</p>
        <p class="small mut mt0">No drinking glasses, Pyrex or window glass, and no nail varnish bottles. If you're on a sack collection, glass can't go in the sack — use a bank or the tip.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Plastic bottles, pots, tubs and trays</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Drinks, milk, detergent, bleach, shampoo and shower gel bottles; yoghurt and margarine pots; meat, ready meal and fruit trays; plant pots. Plastic tubes such as toothpaste and hand cream — squeeze out and put the lid back on.</p>
        <p class="small mut mt0">No black plastic, no film or bags, no pump tops or trigger sprays, no hard plastics or toys. Screw bottle tops back on rather than binning them loose.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Paper</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Newspapers, magazines, catalogues, junk mail, letters, envelopes and greetings cards. Shredded paper only if it's contained inside another paper item — a cereal box or envelope.</p>
        <p class="small mut mt0">No glittery cards or metallic wrapping paper, no sticky labels, nothing food-stained.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Cardboard</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Packaging, cereal and pet food boxes, ready meal sleeves, egg boxes, kitchen and toilet roll tubes. Flatten boxes and tubes.</p>
        <p class="small mut mt0">Take out any film, bags or polystyrene first, and leave greasy pizza boxes for the black bin.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Cartons</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Milk, juice, smoothie, soup, passata, custard and UHT cartons. Flatten them. Plastic spouts can stay on; lids come off but can go in the bin separately.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Black bin — everything else</h3>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="mt0">General household rubbish, <strong>including food waste</strong> — there's no separate food collection here yet.</p>
      <p>Also black plastic, cling film and soft plastics, crisp packets and sweet wrappers, foil pouches, coffee pods, drinking glasses and Pyrex, and pump tops and trigger sprays.</p>
      <p class="small mut mt0">Soft plastics can go to the carrier bag recycling point at larger supermarkets in the meantime. Wychavon expects to collect plastic film from the kerbside from spring 2027.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Alongside the black bin, not in it</h3>
    <div class="grid">
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Batteries</h3>
        <p class="mt0">In a small plastic bag placed <em>on top of</em> the black bin. Crews put them in a separate cage on the lorry. Most supermarkets take them too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Small electricals</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Anything with a plug, a battery or a crossed-out wheelie bin symbol. On top of or beside the bin — never inside it, and never in the recycling.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h3 class="mt0">Textiles</h3>
        <p class="mt0">Clean, dry clothing, bed sheets and towels in a securely tied bag next to the bin, so they survive the rain. Anything still good is better off at a charity shop.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3>Brown bin — garden waste</h3>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="mt0">A <strong>paid subscription</strong> service, so it only applies if you've signed up. Where it runs, it's collected on the same day as the green bin.</p>
      <p><a href="https://www.wychavon.gov.uk/waste-and-recycling/garden-waste-collection-service" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Garden waste collection service at Wychavon &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>
    <p class="small mut">Some rural properties are given sacks rather than wheelie bins. Collection days are the same either way.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Recycling banks nearby</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="mt0">If you have a green bin you don't need these — paper, glass, card and cans all go in the bin. They're useful for sack households and for overflow.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The Fish &amp; Anchor, Evesham Road, Offenham — glass</li>
        <li>Oat Street, Evesham — glass and cans</li>
        <li>Morrisons, Springfield Drive, Evesham — glass and cans</li>
        <li>Tesco, Worcester Road, Evesham — glass and cans</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Nearest household tip</h2>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="mt0"><strong>Hill &amp; Moor</strong>, Piddle Brook Lane, Wyre Piddle WR10 2LW.</p>
      <p>Monday to Saturday 8am&ndash;6pm, Sunday 9am&ndash;1.30pm. No booking needed for cars, but you'll need proof of a Worcestershire address. Opening hours change seasonally, so it's worth checking before you set out.</p>
      <p class="small mut mt0">Vans, trailers and pickups need an e-permit from Worcestershire County Council.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="card">
      <p class="mt0 small muted">Checked against Wychavon District Council and Worcestershire County Council guidance in September 2026. Collection days may change, particularly around Christmas and New Year. If something here looks wrong, please email <a href="mailto:{{ site.email }}">{{ site.email }}</a>, and for a specific item try Wychavon's <a href="https://www.wychavon.gov.uk/waste-and-recycling/recycling/a-to-z-recycling-guide" target="_blank" rel="noopener">A to Z recycling guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<script>
(function () {
  var data = {{ bins | dump | safe }};
  var wrap = document.getElementById('bin-grid');
  if (!wrap || !data || !data.collections || !data.areas) return;

  var colours = { black: '#2f2f2f', green: '#7ab648', brown: '#6b4a2c' };

  var now = new Date();
  var today = new Date(now); today.setHours(0, 0, 0, 0);

  function toDate(s) { var p = s.split('-'); return new Date(+p[0], p[1] - 1, +p[2]); }
  function shift(d, n) { var x = new Date(d); x.setDate(x.getDate() + n); return x; }
  function when(d) {
    return d.getTime() === today.getTime()
      ? 'Today'
      : d.toLocaleDateString('en-GB', { weekday: 'long', day: 'numeric', month: 'long' });
  }
  function label(list) {
    return list.indexOf('black') > -1
      ? 'Black bin'
      : 'Green recycling bin' + (list.indexOf('brown') > -1 ? ' &amp; brown garden bin' : '');
  }

  var html = data.areas.map(function (area) {
    var off = area.offset || 0;
    var found = [];
    for (var i = 0; i < data.collections.length && found.length < 2; i++) {
      var c = data.collections[i];
      var d = shift(toDate(c.date), off);
      var cutoff = new Date(d); cutoff.setHours(10, 0, 0, 0);
      if (cutoff > now) found.push({ date: d, bins: c.bins, note: c.note });
    }
    if (!found.length) return '';

    var n = found[0];
    var swatches = n.bins.map(function (b) {
      return '<div class="bin-swatch" style="background:' + (colours[b] || '#999') + ';"></div>';
    }).join('');

    return '<div class="bin-box">' + swatches +
      '<div><strong>' + area.name + '</strong>' +
      '<div>' + when(n.date) + ' &mdash; ' + label(n.bins) + '</div>' +
      (found[1] ? '<div class="small mut">Then ' + when(found[1].date) + ' &mdash; ' + label(found[1].bins) + '</div>' : '') +
      (n.note ? '<div class="small mut">' + n.note + '</div>' : '') +
      '</div></div>';
  }).join('');

  if (html) wrap.innerHTML = html;
})();
</script>
